From 463c0f632fa0fea99db164fe39a4b5c7c6478ef4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:03:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arch(qwen4exp): enable RS rollback (ring-salvage) for the
 hybrid_idx memory
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The T16 port built the full RS chain (hybrid_idx seq_rm over recr+idx+attn,
ring widened to 1+n_rs_seq incl. the PLE conv row, need_n_rs_seq sizing) but never
listed the arch, so n_rs_seq was clamped to 0 and every partial verify rejection
paid a full checkpoint restore (~115-148 MiB) — the 'speculative replay stalled'
thrashing seen in production at long ctx.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
---
 src/llama-arch.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/llama-arch.cpp b/src/llama-arch.cpp
index b5b595665..da06ebf94 100644
--- a/src/llama-arch.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-arch.cpp
@@ -1079,6 +1079,7 @@ bool llm_arch_supports_rs_rollback(const llm_arch & arch) {
         case LLM_ARCH_QWEN35:
         case LLM_ARCH_QWEN35MOE:
         case LLM_ARCH_DEEPSEEK4:
+        case LLM_ARCH_QWEN4EXP:   // T19: hybrid_idx memory (GDN ring + PLE row + QSA idx) supports per-row rollback
             return true;
         default:
             return false;
-- 
2.43.0

